[al:新概念英语第四册]
[ti:13. Oxford]
[00:00.300] Passage 13 | 文章 13
[00:02.680] Oxford has been ruined by the motor industry. | 牛津已被汽车工业毁坏。
[00:06.955] The peace which Oxford once knew | 牛津曾经的宁静，
[00:09.950] and which a great university city should always have, | 一座伟大的大学城应始终拥有的宁静，
[00:13.290] has been swept ruthlessly away. | 已被无情地扫除。
[00:16.050] And no benefactions and research endowments can make up for the change in character | 任何捐赠和研究捐款都无法弥补其品格上的改变，
[00:21.290] which the city has suffered. | 这座城市因此遭受了苦难。
[00:23.800] At 6 in the morning, | 早上六点，
[00:26.265] the old courts shake to the roar of buses | 古老的庭院在公交车的轰鸣声中颤抖，
[00:28.810] taking the next shift to Cowley, | 载着下一班工人前往考利，
[00:30.750] and pressed steel great lorries with a double deck cargo | 压制钢材的大货车，载着双层货物，
[00:34.109] of cars for export lumber past Magdalen and the University Church. | 满载出口汽车，隆隆地驶过莫德林学院和大学教堂。
[00:39.060] Loads of motor engines are hurried thither and thither, | 一批批汽车发动机被匆匆运往各处，
[00:42.985] and the streets are thronged with a population | 街道上挤满了这样一群人，
[00:45.630] which has no interest in learning, | 他们对学习毫无兴趣，
[00:47.505] and knows no studies beyond servo systems and distributors, | 除了伺服系统和分电器、
[00:50.995] compression ratios and camshafts. | 压缩比和凸轮轴之外，一无所知。
[00:54.330] Theoretically, the marriage of an old seat of learning and tradition | 理论上，一个古老的学习和传统中心，
[00:58.675] with a new and wealthy industry | 与一个新的富裕产业的结合，
[01:00.340] might be expected to produce some interesting children. | 有望产生一些有趣的成果。
[01:04.150] It might have been thought that the culture of the university | 人们可能会认为大学的文化，
[01:07.598] would radiate out and transform the lives of the workers. | 会辐射开来并改变工人的生活。
[01:11.330] That this has not happened | 而这并没有发生，
[01:13.575] may be the fault of the university. | 也许是大学的过错。
[01:15.740] For at both Oxford and Cambridge, the colleges tend to live in an era | 因为在牛津和剑桥，学院们倾向于生活在一个时代，
[01:20.165] which is certainly not of the 20th century, | 这个时代肯定不是20世纪的，
[01:23.335] and upon a planet which bears little resemblance | 并且生活在一个几乎不与
[01:26.125] to the war-torn earth. | 饱受战争蹂躏的地球相似的星球上。
[01:28.245] Wherever the fault may lie, | 无论过错在何方，
[01:30.675] the fact remains | 事实依然是：
[01:32.195] that it is the theatre at Oxford, | 是牛津的剧院，
[01:34.110] and not at Cambridge, | 而不是剑桥的剧院，
[01:35.375] which is on the verge of extinction. | 正处于灭绝的边缘。
[01:37.395] And the only fruit of the combination of industry | 工业结合的唯一成果，
[01:40.470] and the rarefied atmosphere of learning | 以及稀薄的学习氛围，
[01:42.545] is the dust in the streets, | 是街上的尘土，
[01:44.285] and a pathetic sense of being lost | 以及一种可悲的失落感，
[01:46.835] which hangs over some of the colleges. | 萦绕在一些学院上空。
[01:49.670] Roger Pilkington, | 罗杰·皮尔金顿，
[01:51.520] Thames Waters. | 泰晤士河水。